<title>USA: Boise City, Idaho, airports yield 4.65 pct in 2000.</title>
<headline>Boise City, Idaho, airports yield 4.65 pct in 2000.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seattle Northwest Securities Corp said Tuesday it tentatively priced $2.83 million Boise City, Idaho, Airport revenue certificates of participation, series 1996A, at a top yield of 4.65 percent in 2000.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>CITY OF BOISE CITY, IDAHO, AIRPORT REVENUE</p>
<p>CERTIFICATES OF PARTICIPATION, SERIES 1996A</p>
<p>PRESSURE TREATED TIMBER PROJECT</p>
<p>RE: $2,830,000</p>
<p>MOODY'S: A1</p>
<p>S&amp;P: NR</p>
<p>EXPECTED DELIVERY: 10/1/96</p>
<p>DATED: 10/1/96</p>
<p>NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>FIRST COUPON: 2/1/97</p>
<p>    2/1	     Amount	  Coupon	Price</p>
<p>    Maturity	(mln)	   (pct)	 (% of par)</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    1997	    $0.750	  4.50	  3.80</p>
<p>    1998	    $0.675	  4.50	  4.20</p>
<p>    1999	    $0.690	  4.50	  4.45</p>
<p>    2000	    $0.715	  4.50	  4.65</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
